Each site root reads its own type set: `game`, whose `_schemas/` adds `mechanic`, gets the
record page and the type page; `other`, with a `mechanic/` directory but no schema, gets
neither — one record, five pages (index, two root pages, one type page, one record page).

-- fixtures/cwd/game/_schemas/mechanic.yaml --
doc: mechanic

rules:
  - select: FRONTMATTER
    has:
      type: mechanic
      title: '^.+$'
      summary: '^.{1,200}$'
      status: { enum: [draft, accepted] }

  - select: H2
    ordered: [Loop]
    strict: true
-- fixtures/cwd/game/mechanic/0001-dash.md --
---
type: mechanic
title: Dash
summary: A short burst of speed on a cooldown.
status: accepted
---

## Loop

Press, burst, wait for the cooldown.
-- fixtures/cwd/other/mechanic/0001-dash.md --
---
type: mechanic
title: Dash
summary: A short burst of speed on a cooldown.
status: accepted
---

## Loop

Press, burst, wait for the cooldown.
-- cmd --
booping specs site --root game=game --root other=other
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
specs site: 2 roots, 1 records, 9 pages, 0 warnings -> specs-site
-- stderr --
